\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. The people that in darkness lay,
\par In sin and error's deadly shade,
\par Have seen a glorious gospel day
\par In Jesu's lovely face displayed.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thou only, Lord, the work hast done,
\par And bared Thine arm in all our sight;
\par Hast made the reprobates Thine own,
\par And claimed the outcasts as Thy right.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Thine arm alone, almighty Lord,
\par To us the great salvation brought,
\par Thy word, Thy all-creating Word,
\par That spake at first the world from nought.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. For this the saints lift up their voice,
\par And ceaseless praise to Thee  is given;
\par For this the hosts above rejoice;
\par We raise the happiness of heaven.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

